# GLO: the master FX type (what SELECT runs: only that one is active) and the master compressor; the list scrolls
tap GLO
expect view 3
expectselfx 0
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectselfx 1
shot glo_masterfx.png
# SELECT is now the crush amount, and the drive does nothing (it is skipped: its amount stays 0 here and, set, it would not run)
turn SELECT 5
expectfx 3 0 10
expectfx 2 0 0
# the compressor rows: THRESH (95), RATIO (2), ATTACK, RELEASE, MAKEUP, MIX start at the 7th row
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K2 -10
expectcomp 0 75
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectcomp 1 3
turn K1 1
turn K2 5
expectcomp 2 90
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K2 -3
expectcomp 4 6
shot glo_comp.png
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
shot glo_end.png
# GLO has no ENGINE and no VOLUME row any more: the rows are TEMPO, MASTER FX, four knobs, six compressor rows, CLIPS, CPU, BATTERY
